  "body": "Closes #929\nRefs #728 (what is left: the grey skin's stylesheet, which needs a page served to an account with that skin; the operator authorized user2 only tonight, and user2 has the default skin)\nClaim: mac/M1\nAuthor model: opus-5.5 (mac/M1)\nReviewer model: fable-5.2 (mac/M1-r1091-fable: REQUEST CHANGES on cffb7664; APPROVE on 25e1b6b1, the head)\n\n## What\nAll captures are anonymous GETs through `tooling/fixtures/flows.py`, 2026-11-18: 8 requests, 10 s apart, no account.\n\n| Id | What |\n|---|---|\n| `R929a`-`R929d` | `GET /webservices/rest_api.php?uri=forums/hardwarefr/categories/<cat>/subcategories/` for cat 14 (Photo numérique), 4 (Windows & Software), 12 (Graphisme) and 6 (Achats & Ventes): 10, 12, 10 and 11 entries |\n| `R728a` | The default skin's stylesheet: `/include/the_style1.php?color_key=FFFFFF/DEDFDF/…&abs_img_path=…&hide_bg_onglet=0&v=…`, the exact URL the anonymous home page links |\n| `R728b` | The static `https://forum-images.hardware.fr/compressed/the_style.css?v=11102781422` |\n\n## Facts (HFR-PROTOCOL)\n- **#929:** the 7 sub-forums the legacy completion injects there are all still served. Photo numérique « Divers » (457); Windows & Software « Win 9x/Me » (504); Graphisme « Concours » (229), « Ressources » (230) and « Divers » (231); Achats & Ventes « Divers » (174) and « Règles et coutumes » (399). Nothing to remove from `SubforumInjection`; LOT-168 (#286) can check them by id.\n- **#728:**\n  - The skin is chosen by the `color_key` of `the_style1.php`, and it follows the **session**, not the account: the default skin's starts `FFFFFF/DEDFDF/…` (every anonymous and user2 page of the corpus, and user1's pages served outside a logged-in session: `W01`, `W01b`, `R830t`); the grey skin's starts `666666/404550/…` (the 98 pages served to a logged-in user1 session). The grey stylesheet is **not** captured.\n  - The logo `/img/forum_logo.gif` (900 × 71) paints its square and « .FR » in **`#F18F18`**. This is a **run observation** measured on capture `R728l`, which is not committed: the corpus has no binary fixtures and FIXTURES.md no convention for them.\n\n## Anonymization\n- `publish.py` with the local config; `anonymize.py check --corpus`: 733 of 733 clean. The REST answers carry no member data (ids, names, hrefs), and the stylesheets are byte-identical to the raw files.\n- **Independent leak check** (sub-agent `mac/M1-leak337-sonnet`, its own patterns over the raw files): **PASS**.\n- One consistency point, not a leak: the anonymizer mistakes `color_key`'s image-base field (`https%3A%40%40forum-images.hardware.fr`, a public host) for an e-mail, so `R728a.meta.json`'s URL fields carry `…redacted@example.invalid…` and cannot be replayed. Per FIXTURES.md the anonymizer is fixed, not the fixture: #1090.\n\n## Checks\n`python3 -m unittest discover tooling/fixtures/tests` (corpus and MANIFEST agree); the whole HFRKit `swift test` is green on macOS (5 targets), corpus sweeps included; pre-commit green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw\n",
