   "body": "**Adversarial review (fable-5.2, mac/M1-r1091-fable, cffb7664)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES** — doc facts, not the captures (which are clean and correct).\n\n1. **Medium** — `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:611`: \"the grey skin's `666666/404550/…` (every user1 page of the corpus)\" is false. Grep of every committed HTML meta's `account` against its page's `color_key`: user1 → `666666/404550` on 98 pages, but **3 user1 pages carry the default key** `FFFFFF/DEDFDF`: `W01-login-failure.html`, `W01b-login-success-user1.html`, `R830t-rest-bucket-participated-stale-session.html` (all served to a request that is not a logged-in user1 session). Failing scenario: LOT-193 reads this bullet and assumes the key follows the account; a login page or a stale-session page breaks it. Fix: word it \"every page served to a logged-in user1 session (98 of 101); `W01`, `W01b` and `R830t` (not logged in / stale session) carry the default key: the key follows the session, not the account\". Same fix in the PR body.\n\n2. **Medium** — `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:611`: the bullet is tagged **verified**, whose legend (line 5) means \"confirmed by a committed fixture\". The logo colour `#F18F18` rests on `R728l`, not committed, and on a pixel measurement nobody can replay from the repo. Precedent at line 735 / line 612: **run observation**. Fix: split the logo sentence out as \"**run observation** (capture `R728l`, binary, not committed; FIXTURES.md has no binary convention: open an issue or note it on #734)\", keep **verified** for the two stylesheets and the `color_key` prefixes (visible in the corpus).\n\n3. **Detail** — `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:611`, `MANIFEST.md:225`: \"every page links two stylesheets\" — the AJAX smiley answers (`R53a`-`c`), `.hop` refusals (`W17b`, `W64x`), 404s and `R98a` link none. \"every full forum page\".\n\n4. **Detail** — `MANIFEST.md:224`: `R728a`'s URL carries the redacted host (#1090); the row could say so, as the protocol bullet does, so a reader does not replay it as is.\n\n`Closes #929` is right: the follow-up test belongs to #286 (LOT-168, open, `Blocked by #929`), which this unblocks. `Refs #728` right (grey stylesheet left).\n\n**Verified** (worktree of cffb7664, removed after): the 7 injected sub-forums are present by id and name in `R929a`-`R929d` with counts 10/12/10/11, `list_type`/`page`/`results_count` as stated, and match `SubforumInjection.swift:40-63`; `R728a`/`R728b` hold no `redacted`/`example.invalid`; ids `R728a-b`, `R929a-d` unused on `dev-swift`; corpus.d fragment format per README; `python3 -m unittest discover tooling/fixtures/tests` OK (corpus and MANIFEST agree); `anonymize.py check --corpus`: 733/733 clean; `swift test --filter OracleOwnershipTests` passed; `pre-commit run --files` on the diff: green. Not run: raw captures, local config (as instructed).\n\n---\nAgent: mac/M1-r1091-fable (Fable), posted verbatim by mac/M1.\n\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
